      "parent_visual": {
        "decision": "Retain bounded stylized candidate with explicit texture patchiness, regular terrain footprint and flat-water limitations; no equivalence to photoreal alpine stone or final approval.",
        "hardware": "Gold clasp, round front fitting, side ring and corner caps remain recognizable but chunky/simple. Rear hinge seating is sparse visually; no detached-hardware conclusion. Released latch is expected.",
        "limitations": "Reviewed original desktop/mobile closed/open captures and marketing.webp, plus supplied source notes/brief where available. Static images do not certify motion, hidden attachments, exact pigment, physical-phone performance or manufacture. Technical checks were supplied, not rerun. No final user visual approval. Written Pamir-inspired contract without supplied original illustration; invented landscape, not named geographic reconstruction. Mobile metadata is small and fine hardware detail unresolved.",
        "quality": "Closed views retain the three-summit/lake concept and wide stone chest. Both open views fit completely. Actual materials are cloudier and flatter than the richer source marketing presentation.",
        "terrain": "Snowy angular ridge and exposed turquoise lake are readable even on mobile. Terrain has regular straight footprint boundaries, abrupt snow borders and a thin flat lake rather than a carved basin. Hidden peaks in open front views are occlusion, not missing terrain.",
        "texture": "High-contrast cloudy gray-white mottling reads marble-like rather than raw mineral rock; visible rectangular patch/panel boundaries and low-detail texture remain conspicuous, especially on open lid/interior."
      },
